{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1095683-dark-ages-and-mage-20","id":1095683,"title":"Dark Ages and Mage 20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-22T17:49:26-07:00","id":1095683,"title":"Dark Ages and Mage 20","content":"Out of curiosity, before I go kitbashing rules together myself, has anyone put out something that uses Foundations like in Dark Ages Mage with Spheres and such from M20? I like the Foundations from M20 but I am not such a big fan of Pillars, I prefer Spheres. Considering I am going to running a Dark Ages game here soon, I was looking at putting some coherent rules on paper so that if any of my players really comes up with a kick ass reason (and maybe a good solid bribe lol) I have some ready.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/690-fenris","name":"Fenris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T18:11:52-07:00","id":1095693,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone's done any formal reworking like you describe. I admit, I've thought of doing something similar. I imagine quite a few people have.<br /> <br /> I think maybe what I'd recommend is creating the character using Dark Age Mage's system first, then sketch out the pillars that you would have chosen for the character. Then you break down the levels of the pillars into what spheres you would use to get a similar effect.<br /> <br /> Then you just give the character those spheres. My guess is that you'll end up with a character that's a little stronger than a starting Ascension character would be, in terms of amount and level of spheres. But that might suit the setting. Mages were supposed to be more powerful back then. Then just use sphere rating to replace pillar rating in the standard system.<br /> <br /> After that, I'd use the pillars as maybe a role playing guide. You could offer some kind of difficulty reduction if the players match their effects to the idea of the pillar, even if they're not using the mechanics, or give them some increased difficulty if they cross into a different Fellowship's style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T02:23:38-07:00","id":1095805,"title":"","content":"I haven't fully written it up, but something I've toyed with to do a &quot;build your own Foundations&quot; system that can be used with Arete and really any historical time period if you want to keep Arete/Spheres as the base system:<br /> <br /> For every dot in Arete, provide an appropriate Background or Merit (that's gotta wait a bit until Book of Secrets finally drops if you want to stick solely to M20 material) equal to the dots in Arete purchased. This can also be used to upgrade existing traits that have scaled values.<br /> <br /> This can be pre-built as Foundations, or free-built in play to more closely match an individual mage's beliefs being made manifest. It also makes the price-tag of Arete a bit more bearable.<br /> <br /> After a bit of testing, I've waffled on possibly cutting down to (Arete - 1) dots of free stuff, since it can get a bit overwhelming at higher XP, and it works better if you set starting Arete at 2 or 3 and don't allow it to be bought with freebies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T11:18:18-07:00","id":1095977,"title":"","content":"I do like M:tDA, and I like the creativity that went into it, but I just like M:tA systems more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T07:18:52-07:00","id":1096301,"title":"","content":"So I guess I get to do it the fun way, yay.<br /> <br /> <br /> Right now for a base I am thinking renaming Arete to Foundation, and letting rolls for magick be Foundation + Sphere with a cap of Willpower. Foundation would become a combination of Arete and Focus from M20, with the write ups in Dark Ages Mage being a good jump off point for basic broad styles, and letting players use a Pillar or twos fluff as a way to round out their Foundation to represent a more localized version of the broad Fellowships.<br /> <br /> With the potential to have more in a Foundation+Sphere dice pool than you have willpower, I am toying with the idea of that lowering the difficulty of what you are doing, to kind of represent the mages that do not have the raw power, but who are very skilled at applying what they do know.<br /> <br /> Still toying the idea of tying Resonance in, I like it in combination with Essences as a way to individualize a mage, and since the entire idea of mage (to me) is finding ways to do reality your way, even when Consensus or Reality itself would prefer it happen a different way, it seems like a good way to make a system that boosts that without having to continually burn Tass to get certain things done, but at the same time, also represents the self reinforcing trap of hubris and tunnel vision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/690-fenris","name":"Fenris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T12:39:42-07:00","id":1096446,"title":"","content":"I'd say that a Foundation would equate to attaching a one-to-five dot rating to a Practice. You roll Practice + Sphere to work an effect, and pay an extra Quintessence if the highest required Sphere is higher than your Practice. (Spheres can go up to 5, and are not capped by Practice; so dice pools are capped at ten dice.) Make liberal use of the Practice's associated Abilities to assist your castings, and don't Surpass your Instruments. You get to \u201cSurpass\u201d two of your seven Instruments for every Practice dot after the first. But don't think of this as Surpassing the Instruments, think of it as Mastering them: using an Instrument that you've Mastered reduces the Effect's difficulty by one. <i>Not using your Instruments</i> shouldn't be a thing with dot-rated Practices. <br /> <br /> Pay close attention to the Paradox rules. DA:Mage handles Scourge the way MRev handles Paradox (e.g., one Paradox per dot in your highest Sphere), so you should decide whether you want to do the same or if you want to use M20's Paradox rules. My preference would be something closer to the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}